{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25616834",
      "title": "Data Fetching for Static Pages",
      "sourceHash": "fb31487ac01a0df8228687782f8954c2f5ce695e95ef449cf0683fa0f8c15f54",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.05,
          "end": 5.46,
          "en": "NextJS has this built-in page pre-rendering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.46,
          "end": 8.64,
          "en": "but this built-in process has a flaw",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.64,
          "end": 10.46,
          "en": "if you wanna call it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.46,
          "end": 12.81,
          "en": "As I showed you a couple of seconds ago,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.81,
          "end": 16.78,
          "en": "the page that is pre-rendered has basically the snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.78,
          "end": 21.26,
          "en": "after the first component render cycle as its content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.26,
          "end": 23.64,
          "en": "and that might be missing crucial data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.64,
          "end": 25.47,
          "en": "So if we visit some route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.47,
          "end": 29.84,
          "en": "if some request is sent to some route to this page then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.84,
          "end": 32.17,
          "en": "there we return that pre-rendered page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.17,
          "end": 34.4,
          "en": "but we might be missing data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.4,
          "end": 37.71,
          "en": "So whilst this is theoretically good for SEO,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.71,
          "end": 39.36,
          "en": "for search engine optimization,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.36,
          "end": 41.17,
          "en": "it might not always be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.17,
          "end": 44.18,
          "en": "But after this HTML page was received,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.18,
          "end": 46.44,
          "en": "React will actually take over,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.44,
          "end": 49.93,
          "en": "the page is hydrated as this process is called,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.93,
          "end": 52.11,
          "en": "which means that now React will turn this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.11,
          "end": 55.83,
          "en": "into a single page application and take over control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.83,
          "end": 59.62,
          "en": "and then this useEffect function might be executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.62,
          "end": 63.4,
          "en": "data might be fetched and the page might be updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.4,
          "end": 66.05,
          "en": "in the browser, not on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.05,
          "end": 67.88,
          "en": "not on the pre-rendered page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.88,
          "end": 72.18,
          "en": "but instead, after this page was received in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.18,
          "end": 74.97,
          "en": "And therefore, we then have a fully interactive page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.97,
          "end": 77.98,
          "en": "or app with all the data we need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.98,
          "end": 81.33,
          "en": "But if we wanna pre-render a page with data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.33,
          "end": 84.89,
          "en": "so that this initially returned HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.89,
          "end": 86.74,
          "en": "already contains the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.74,
          "end": 90.82,
          "en": "we need to fine tune this built-it pre-rendering process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.82,
          "end": 92.72999999999999,
          "en": "and we need to configure it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.72999999999999,
          "end": 97.03,
          "en": "And for this, NextJS gives us two forms of pre-rendering,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.03,
          "end": 100.58,
          "en": "which we can use for controlling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.58,
          "end": 103.47,
          "en": "how the pages should be rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.47,
          "end": 106.75,
          "en": "It has something which is called Static Generation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.75,
          "end": 108.53,
          "en": "and it has an alternative,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.53,
          "end": 111.00999999999999,
          "en": "which is called Server-side Rendering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.00999999999999,
          "end": 113.53999999999999,
          "en": "And the two might sound similar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.53999999999999,
          "end": 118.11,
          "en": "but they run or the code runs at different points of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.11,
          "end": 120.89,
          "en": "as you will learn over the next minutes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.89,
          "end": 123.71,
          "en": "Now, we're going to start with Static Generation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.71,
          "end": 127.15,
          "en": "because that is the approach which you typically should use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.15,
          "end": 128.593,
          "en": "but how does it work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.5,
          "end": 131.83,
          "en": "When using Static Generation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.83,
          "end": 134.51,
          "en": "a page component is pre-rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.51,
          "end": 136.98,
          "en": "when you build your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.98,
          "end": 139.07,
          "en": "when you build the next project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.07,
          "end": 141.89,
          "en": "So when you build it for production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.89,
          "end": 143.2,
          "en": "And that's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 143.2,
          "end": 145.18,
          "en": "With Static Generation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 145.18,
          "end": 148.96,
          "en": "by default, your page is not pre-rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 148.96,
          "end": 151.13,
          "en": "on the fly on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 151.13,
          "end": 153.9,
          "en": "when a request reaches the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 153.9,
          "end": 155.9,
          "en": "but instead, it is pre-rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 155.9,
          "end": 160.73,
          "en": "when you as a developer build your site for production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.73,
          "end": 163.86,
          "en": "And that means that after it was deployed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 163.86,
          "end": 166.82,
          "en": "that pre-rendered page does not change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 166.82,
          "end": 169,
          "en": "At least not by default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 169,
          "end": 171.45,
          "en": "If you then updated the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 171.45,
          "end": 174.99,
          "en": "and you know that the pre-rendered page needs to change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 174.99,
          "end": 177.82,
          "en": "you need to start that build process again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 177.82,
          "end": 179.64,
          "en": "and redeploy again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 179.64,
          "end": 182.24,
          "en": "But that might sound worse than it actually is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 182.24,
          "end": 184.62,
          "en": "because for a lot of applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 184.62,
          "end": 186.53,
          "en": "pages don't change all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 186.53,
          "end": 188.8,
          "en": "Page content doesn't change all the time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 188.8,
          "end": 191.28,
          "en": "and if it should change frequently,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 191.28,
          "end": 194.04,
          "en": "there are alternatives, which I will also show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 194.04,
          "end": 195.377,
          "en": "in a couple of minutes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 195.377,
          "end": 199.188,
          "en": "But for the moment, let's start with this Static Generation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 199.188,
          "end": 201.57,
          "en": "Now, as I mentioned, by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 201.57,
          "end": 203.7,
          "en": "NextJS prepares your pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 203.7,
          "end": 207.27,
          "en": "It by default generates your pages already statically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 207.27,
          "end": 210.9,
          "en": "and it by default does that during the build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 210.9,
          "end": 213.66,
          "en": "but if you need to wait for data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 213.66,
          "end": 216.98,
          "en": "if you need to add data fetching to a page component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 216.98,
          "end": 221.27,
          "en": "you can do so by exporting a special function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 221.27,
          "end": 223.92000000000002,
          "en": "from inside your page component file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 223.92000000000002,
          "end": 225.87,
          "en": "And that's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 225.87,
          "end": 229.41,
          "en": "This now only works in your page component files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 229.41,
          "end": 231.67000000000002,
          "en": "not in other component files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 231.67000000000002,
          "end": 235.82,
          "en": "Only in component files inside of the pages folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 235.82,
          "end": 238.36,
          "en": "In there, you can export a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 238.36,
          "end": 240.62,
          "en": "a function called getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 242.29,
          "end": 245.503,
          "en": "and it has to be called getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 246.65,
          "end": 249.37,
          "en": "This is a reserved name so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 249.37,
          "end": 252.67,
          "en": "NextJS will look for a function with that name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 252.67,
          "end": 256.38,
          "en": "and if it finds it, it executes this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 256.38,
          "end": 259.623,
          "en": "during this pre-rendering process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 260.58,
          "end": 264.2,
          "en": "So it will then not directly call your component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 264.2,
          "end": 268.68,
          "en": "and use the returned JSX snapshot as HTML content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 268.68,
          "end": 271.77,
          "en": "but it will, first of all, call getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 271.77,
          "end": 274.52,
          "en": "before it calls the component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 274.52,
          "end": 277.56,
          "en": "And getStaticProps has this name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 277.56,
          "end": 282.56,
          "en": "because indeed, its job is to prepare props for this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 284.05,
          "end": 288.39,
          "en": "And these props could then contain the data this page needs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 288.39,
          "end": 291.49,
          "en": "And that's useful because getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 291.49,
          "end": 294.04,
          "en": "is allowed to be asynchronous.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 294.04,
          "end": 296.22,
          "en": "You can return a promise there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 296.22,
          "end": 298.45,
          "en": "and then, and that's the key thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 298.45,
          "end": 302.4,
          "en": "NextJS will wait for this promise to resolve,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 302.4,
          "end": 305.2,
          "en": "which means it waits until your data is loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 305.2,
          "end": 309.79,
          "en": "and then you return the props for this component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 309.79,
          "end": 312.25,
          "en": "And with that, you're able to load data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 312.25,
          "end": 314.95,
          "en": "before this component function is executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 314.95,
          "end": 317.42,
          "en": "so that this component can be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 317.42,
          "end": 318.973,
          "en": "with the required data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 320.22,
          "end": 322.34,
          "en": "Now, here in getStaticProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 322.34,
          "end": 324.5,
          "en": "you can also execute any code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 324.5,
          "end": 327.73,
          "en": "that would normally only run on a server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 327.73,
          "end": 329.88,
          "en": "You could access a file system here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 329.88,
          "end": 332.74,
          "en": "or securely connect to a database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 332.74,
          "end": 335.15999999999997,
          "en": "because any code you write in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 335.15999999999997,
          "end": 337.57,
          "en": "will never end up on the client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 337.57,
          "end": 341.05,
          "en": "and it will never execute on the client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 341.05,
          "end": 344.40999999999997,
          "en": "simply because this code is executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 344.40999999999997,
          "end": 345.92,
          "en": "during the build process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 345.92,
          "end": 350.06,
          "en": "not on the server and especially not on the clients",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 350.06,
          "end": 351.73,
          "en": "of your visitors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 351.73,
          "end": 355.1,
          "en": "So the code in here will never reach the machines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 355.1,
          "end": 356.35,
          "en": "of your visitors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 356.35,
          "end": 359.35,
          "en": "It will never execute on their machines.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 359.35,
          "end": 361.12,
          "en": "Now, here in getStaticProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 361.12,
          "end": 362.45,
          "en": "you can do whatever you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 362.45,
          "end": 366.48,
          "en": "for example, fetch data from an API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 366.48,
          "end": 369.88,
          "en": "or from a database or read data from some files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 369.88,
          "end": 371.97,
          "en": "in the file system, like we do it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 371.97,
          "end": 375.2,
          "en": "in my full NextJS course, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 375.2,
          "end": 378.03,
          "en": "But then once you're done with whatever you did",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 378.03,
          "end": 379.84,
          "en": "to get the data you need,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 379.84,
          "end": 383.183,
          "en": "you need to return an object here in getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 384.04,
          "end": 387.072,
          "en": "You always need to return an object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 387.072,
          "end": 388.83,
          "en": "Now, in this object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 388.83,
          "end": 390.93,
          "en": "you can configure various things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 390.93,
          "end": 392.5,
          "en": "but most importantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 392.5,
          "end": 396.2,
          "en": "you typically set a props property here",
